WEBVTT

00:05:58.236 --> 00:06:01.996
And with the rapid innovation of molecular
and computational tools,

00:06:02.036 --> 00:06:05.356
we are finally getting
a sneak peek at who they are

00:06:05.356 --> 00:06:07.316
and how they make their way in the world.

00:06:07.356 --> 00:06:08.636
Here's the thing.

00:06:08.636 --> 00:06:12.356
A teaspoon of soil
holds billions of organisms,

00:06:12.396 --> 00:06:15.796
things like bacteria, fungi,
protists and archaea.

00:06:16.196 --> 00:06:19.116
These microbes
are the movers and shakers

00:06:19.156 --> 00:06:20.796
of nature's carbon cycle.

00:06:20.836 --> 00:06:23.876
They drive really important
processes in soil,

00:06:23.916 --> 00:06:25.316
they take organic matter

00:06:25.356 --> 00:06:28.276
and convert it into complex
carbon molecules.

00:06:28.796 --> 00:06:32.436
And having more carbon in soil
is transformative.